    theory: ['In this tutorial, we will learn how to use a ttf font file in Matplotlib. We will use the Computer Modern Roman font (cmr10) shipped with Matplotlib to display a special font in the plot. If you face issues during learning, feel free to ask Labby. Provide feedback after the session, and we will promptly resolve the problem for you. In this tutorial, we learned how to use a ttf font file in Matplotlib to display a special font in the plot. We used the set_title() method to set the font for the title of the plot and passed the font path as the font parameter. We need to import matplotlib.pyplot and matplotlib to create and display the plot. We create a plot using the subplots() method and store the figure and axes objects in fig and ax variables respectively. Source: matplotlib/matplotlib · by huduo0812 · BSD 3-Clause.'],
